  "body": "From the merge-order analysis of 2026-11-22. Most text conflicts between open PRs are in a small set of registry files. Each new post, machine, MCP tool or operation kind adds a line near the same place:\n\n- `crates/app/src/posting_files.rs`, `crates/app/src/posting.rs` (post lists)\n- `crates/post/tests/conformance.rs`, `comment_escape.rs` (one row for each post)\n- `crates/post/src/lib.rs`\n- `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` (a generated table)\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`, `cam.d.ts`\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/mod.rs`\n\nThirteen PRs of the Agie chain and five new-post PRs conflict with each other only in these files.\n\n## Necessary work (each item can be its own PR)\n1. Posts: find the shipped posts from `assets/posts/` (or one small file for each post), so that a new post adds a file and changes no shared list.\n2. Conformance and comment-escape tests: one row source for each post next to the post, read by the test.\n3. Lists that stay in code: one entry for each line, sorted, with a test that fails when the list is not sorted.\n4. `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md`: make it again at merge time from the tool list (a `cargo xtask` command that the merging session runs), or give it `merge=union` in `.gitattributes`. Choose one and record why.\n\n## Done means\n- Two branches that each add a post merge with no conflict in a test of `cargo xtask merge-plan`.\n- No behaviour change: the posts, the goldens and the MCP tool list are the same.\n",
